  "item": "ch05.s10",
  "inputs_hash": "7f8daca39805409e4b0331320c089c9eeaca03a9b9bba3775845dad2d2ef7e56",
  "output_hash": "04be7c4cd64fff0fcc70d0644dce6d4c0578fc57d9b7073eea8393f8168ea54b",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch05.s10",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch05.s10.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p01.r01",
            "text": "How can a pretrained GPT model be turned into something that decides whether a message is spam or not, and how do its outputs become a class label?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p01.r02",
            "text": "For this classification task, the original final output layer took 768 inputs, matching the embedding dimension, and produced 50,257 outputs, matching the vocabulary size.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@221",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@224",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@225",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@228"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p01.r03",
            "text": "That layer is replaced with a classification head that still takes 768 inputs but produces 2 outputs, for spam or no spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@231",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@234",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@238",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@240",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@242",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@244"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p01.r04",
            "text": "Attaching this classification head on top of the GPT architecture allows the model to be used for a classification task.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2733",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2735",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2740",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2742"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p01.r05",
            "text": "Fine-tuning requires changing the GPT model architecture so that the model answers better and its accuracy improves.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2869",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2872",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2874",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2876",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2878"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s10.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p02.01",
            "text": "Once the architecture is modified, a sequence input produces outputs at every token position.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p02.02",
            "text": "For example, if the input is \"do you have time\", each token produces two outputs corresponding to spam or no spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@256",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@258",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@265",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@268",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@270",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@277",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@281",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@283"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p02.03",
            "text": "With one sample containing four tokens, the output tensor has shape 1 x 4 x 2: one batch element, four tokens, and two outputs per token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@306",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@308",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@311",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@314",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@317",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@319",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@322",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@325",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@326",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@329"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p02.04",
            "text": "For classification, only the output of the last token is used, because the last token contains information about the other tokens through its attention weights.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@288",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@290",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@292",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@294",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@296",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@298",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@301"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p02.05",
            "text": "The final output used for the decision is therefore the pair of values produced by that last token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@338",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@339",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@342",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@344",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@347"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s10.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p03.r01",
            "text": "The next step is to turn those two final values into a predicted label.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p03.r02",
            "text": "The procedure is to take the last-token outputs, apply softmax to convert them into probabilities, and then choose the index with the highest value.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@400",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@402",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@413",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@415",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@417",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@423",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@426"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p03.r03",
            "text": "For example, one message can produce probabilities 0.99 and 0.01 after softmax, and then the predicted class is index 0, which means no spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@419",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@423",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@426",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@431",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@434",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@437",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@440"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p03.r04",
            "text": "Another message can produce probabilities 0.01 and 0.99 after softmax, and then the predicted class is index 1, which means spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@442",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@445",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@452",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@454",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@457",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@460",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@462",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@464"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p03.r05",
            "text": "Applying softmax is unnecessary when only the predicted class is needed, because the index of the largest logit is the same as the index of the highest probability.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@468",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@469",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@472",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@475",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@477",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@480",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@483",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@485",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@545",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@548",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@550",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@551"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s10.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p04.r01",
            "text": "A concrete pair of logits makes the conversion clear.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p04.r02",
            "text": "For a last-token output of -3.5983 and 3.9902, the code applies softmax, prints the resulting probabilities, and then uses argmax to find the class label.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@493",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@495",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@497",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@501",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@503",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@505",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@508",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@512",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@516",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@531",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@533"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p04.r03",
            "text": "In that example, one printed softmax value is 0.9995.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@526"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s10.p04.r04",
            "text": "Because 0.9995 is larger, argmax returns class label 1, so the model predicts that the input text is spam.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@526",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@528",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@531",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@535",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@536",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@539",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@541",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@543"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
